module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.JacobianCriterionNodal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.CotangentBasis
import all StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.JacobianCriterionPlane
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The Jacobian criterion in two variables, for an arbitrary family of equations

Let `k` be a field, `B = k[[x_0, x_1]]` and `J ⊆ 𝔪_B ^ 2` the ideal generated by a finite family
`h`. This file proves that the partial derivatives of the `h j` generate `𝔪_B` modulo `J` exactly
when `B / J` carries a nondegenerate quadratic relation on its cotangent space, that is, exactly
when the quadratic parts of the elements of `J` contain a nondegenerate binary quadratic form.

This is the `n = 2` case of Stacks 0C4C with no restriction on the number of equations. The
single-equation case is `Stacks.Curves.span_pderiv_eq_maximalIdeal_iff`; the step from one
equation to a family is exactly the step from a single quadratic form to a *space* of quadratic
forms, which is `Stacks.Curves.span_derivSet_eq_top_iff_exists_nondegenerate`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Curves.linPart` — the pair of linear coefficients of a power series in two variables.
* `Stacks.Curves.quadPart` — the coefficient triple of its quadratic part.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Curves.sup_sq_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_span_linPart` — an ideal generated by elements of
  `𝔪_B` generates `𝔪_B` modulo `𝔪_B ^ 2` exactly when the linear parts of the generators span.
* `Stacks.Curves.span_linPart_image_pderiv_eq_span_derivSet` — the linear parts of the partial
  derivatives of a family span the same subspace as the derivative set of the space spanned by
  the quadratic parts of the family.
* `Stacks.Curves.span_pderiv_sup_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_exists_nondegenerate` — the partial
  derivatives of the family generate `𝔪_B` modulo `J` exactly when some element of `J` has
  nondegenerate quadratic part.
* `Stacks.Curves.quadPart_mul` — the quadratic part of a product of two elements of `𝔪_B` is the
  product of their linear parts as binary quadratic forms. This is what makes the discriminant
  transform by the square of a determinant under a change of the two generators of `𝔪_B`.
* `Stacks.Curves.exists_quadratic_decomposition` — an element of `𝔪_B ^ 2` is a combination of
  the three quadratic monomials whose coefficients have the quadratic part as constant terms.
* `Stacks.Curves.exists_nondegenerate_quadPart_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation` — that condition is
  exactly `Stacks.Curves.HasNodalQuadraticRelation` for `B / J`.
* `Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation` — the
  two combined, in the vocabulary of Tag 0C4B.
* `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_jacobianMinorIdeal_tfae_two_of_le_sq` — **Tag 0C4C for `n = 2`
  and `I ⊆ 𝔪_A ^ 2`**, obtained from the previous result and
  `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_tfae_of_jacobianMinorIdeal_iff`.

## Implementation notes

The linear and quadratic parts are `k`-linear maps into `k × k` and `k × k × k`, the latter being
the coefficient model of binary quadratic forms used by
`Stacks.Curves.quadDisc` and `Stacks.Curves.derivSet`. That the quadratic part of a multiple
`c * g` of an element `g ∈ 𝔪 ^ 2` is the constant term of `c` times that of `g` is the statement
that `𝔪 · 𝔪 ^ 2 ⊆ 𝔪 ^ 3` together with
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.coeff_eq_zero_of_mem_pow_maximalIdeal`; no graded structure
  on the power-series ring
is introduced.

Several linear-coefficient helpers of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.JacobianCriterionPlane` are private, so that module is
imported with `import all` rather than having them re-proved here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4C)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing MvPowerSeries

namespace Stacks.Curves

universe u

variable {k : Type u} [Field k]

/-! ### The linear and quadratic parts -/

/-- The pair of linear coefficients of a power series in two variables. -/
noncomputable def linPart : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k →ₗ[k] k × k :=
  (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 1)).prod
    (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 1 1))

/-- The coefficient triple `(a, b, c)` of the quadratic part `a x_0 ^ 2 + b x_0 x_1 + c x_1 ^ 2`
of a power series in two variables. -/
noncomputable def quadPart : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k →ₗ[k] k × k × k :=
  (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 2)).prod
    ((MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1)).prod
      (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 1 2)))

/-- The linear part of `g` is the pair of its coefficients of `x_0` and `x_1`. -/
theorem linPart_apply (g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    linPart g = (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 1) g,
      MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 1 1) g) := rfl

/-- The quadratic part of `g` is the triple of its coefficients of `x_0 ^ 2`, `x_0 x_1` and
`x_1 ^ 2`. -/
theorem quadPart_apply (g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    quadPart g = (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 2) g,
      MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1) g,
      MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 1 2) g) := rfl

/-- An element of `𝔪` lies in `𝔪 ^ 2` exactly when its linear part vanishes. -/
theorem mem_sq_iff_linPart_eq_zero {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 ↔ linPart g = 0 := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
      simpa [linPart_apply, ← linCoeff_eq_coeff] using linCoeff_eq_zero_of_mem_sq _ h
  · intro h
    refine Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_sq_maximalIdeal_of_linear_coeff_zero _
      ((Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field _).1
        hg) ?_
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simpa [linPart_apply] using congrArg Prod.fst h
    · simpa [linPart_apply] using congrArg (fun p : k × k => p.2) h

/-- An element of `𝔪 ^ 3` has vanishing quadratic part. -/
theorem quadPart_eq_zero_of_mem_cube {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 3) : quadPart g = 0 := by
  have hdeg : ∀ d : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ, (∑ i, d i) < 3 → MvPowerSeries.coeff d g = 0 :=
    fun d hd => Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.coeff_eq_zero_of_mem_pow_maximalIdeal hg d hd
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;> simp only [quadPart_apply]
  · exact hdeg _ (by simp)
  · exact hdeg _ (by simp [Finsupp.single_apply])
  · exact hdeg _ (by simp)

/-- The coordinate `x_i` lies in the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem X_mem_maximalIdeal (i : Fin 2) :
    (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
  (Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field _).2
    (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff_X i)

/-- A product of two elements of `𝔪` lies in `𝔪 ^ 2`. -/
private theorem mul_mem_sq {a b : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (ha : a ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k))
    (hb : b ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    a * b ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := by
  rw [pow_two]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul ha hb

/-- A product of an element of `𝔪` and an element of `𝔪 ^ 2` lies in `𝔪 ^ 3`. -/
private theorem mul_mem_cube {a b : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (ha : a ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k))
    (hb : b ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) :
    a * b ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 3 := by
  rw [show (3 : ℕ) = 1 + 2 from rfl, pow_add, pow_one]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul ha hb

/-- The family of generators spans an ideal inside `𝔪 ^ 2` when each generator lies in `𝔪 ^ 2`. -/
private theorem span_range_le_sq {m : ℕ} {h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hh : ∀ j, h j ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range h) ≤ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 :=
  Ideal.span_le.2 (Set.forall_mem_range.2 hh)

/-- Subtracting the constant term of a power series leaves an element of `𝔪`. -/
private theorem sub_C_constantCoeff_mem (c : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    c - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c) ∈
      maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
  (Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field _).2
    (by simp)

/-- The linear part of a multiple of an element of `𝔪` is the constant term of the multiplier
times the linear part. -/
theorem linPart_mul_of_mem {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) (c : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    linPart (c * g) = MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c • linPart g := by
  have hmem := mul_mem_sq (sub_C_constantCoeff_mem c) hg
  have hzero : linPart ((c - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c)) * g) = 0 :=
    (mem_sq_iff_linPart_eq_zero (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) hmem)).1 hmem
  have hsplit : c * g =
      MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c) * g +
        (c - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c)) * g := by ring
  rw [hsplit, map_add, hzero, add_zero]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp [linPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_C_mul]

/-- The quadratic part of a multiple of an element of `𝔪 ^ 2` is the constant term of the
multiplier times the quadratic part. -/
theorem quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) (c : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    quadPart (c * g) = MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c • quadPart g := by
  have hmem := mul_mem_cube (sub_C_constantCoeff_mem c) hg
  have hsplit : c * g =
      MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c) * g +
        (c - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c)) * g := by ring
  rw [hsplit, map_add, quadPart_eq_zero_of_mem_cube hmem, add_zero]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;> simp [quadPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_C_mul]

/-! ### Linear and quadratic parts of an ideal -/

/-- Induction on membership in an ideal generated by elements of `P`, for a linear map `f` that
scales by the constant term of the multiplier on `P`. -/
private theorem mem_and_map_mem_span_image {P : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)} {M : Type*}
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module k M] (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k →ₗ[k] M)
    (hf : ∀ g ∈ P, ∀ c : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k,
      f (c * g) = MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c • f g)
    {S : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)} (hS : ∀ g ∈ S, g ∈ P)
    {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k} (hx : x ∈ Ideal.span S) :
    x ∈ P ∧ f x ∈ Submodule.span k (f '' S) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem g hg => exact ⟨hS g hg, Submodule.subset_span ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩⟩
  | zero => exact ⟨Submodule.zero_mem _, by rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _⟩
  | add a b _ _ ha hb =>
    exact ⟨Submodule.add_mem _ ha.1 hb.1, by
      rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha.2 hb.2⟩
  | smul c a _ ha =>
    refine ⟨Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ _ ha.1, ?_⟩
    rw [smul_eq_mul, hf a ha.1]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ha.2

/-- The linear part of an element of an ideal generated by elements of `𝔪` lies in the span of
the linear parts of the generators. -/
theorem linPart_mem_span_image {S : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    (hS : ∀ g ∈ S, g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k))
    {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k} (hx : x ∈ Ideal.span S) :
    x ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ∧
      linPart x ∈ Submodule.span k (linPart '' S) :=
  mem_and_map_mem_span_image (P := maximalIdeal _) linPart
    (fun _ hg c => linPart_mul_of_mem hg c) hS hx

/-- The quadratic part of an element of an ideal generated by elements of `𝔪 ^ 2` lies in the
span of the quadratic parts of the generators. -/
theorem quadPart_mem_span_image {S : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    (hS : ∀ g ∈ S, g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2)
    {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k} (hx : x ∈ Ideal.span S) :
    x ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 ∧
      quadPart x ∈ Submodule.span k (quadPart '' S) :=
  mem_and_map_mem_span_image (M := k × k × k)
    (P := (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) quadPart
    (fun _ hg c => quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq hg c) hS hx

/-! ### Nakayama in two variables -/

private theorem single_one_one_ne_single_zero_one :
    (Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 2) 1 : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ) ≠ Finsupp.single (0 : Fin 2) 1 := by
  intro h
  simpa using congrArg (fun e : Fin 2 →₀ ℕ => e 1) h

/-- The linear part of `x_0` is `(1, 0)`. -/
theorem linPart_X_zero :
    linPart (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) = (1, 0) := by
  simp [linPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_X, single_one_one_ne_single_zero_one]

/-- The linear part of `x_1` is `(0, 1)`. -/
theorem linPart_X_one :
    linPart (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) = (0, 1) := by
  simp [linPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_X, single_one_one_ne_single_zero_one.symm]

/-- **Nakayama in two variables, read on linear parts.** An ideal generated by elements of `𝔪`
generates `𝔪` modulo `𝔪 ^ 2` exactly when the linear parts of its generators span the plane. -/
theorem sup_sq_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_span_linPart {S : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    (hS : ∀ g ∈ S, g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    Ideal.span S ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 =
        maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ↔
      Submodule.span k (linPart '' S) = ⊤ := by
  have hSle : Ideal.span S ≤ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := Ideal.span_le.mpr hS
  constructor
  · intro hsup
    have hX : ∀ i : Fin 2, linPart (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ∈
        Submodule.span k (linPart '' S) := by
      intro i
      obtain ⟨a, ha, b, hb, hab⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 (hsup ▸ X_mem_maximalIdeal i)
      rw [← hab, map_add,
        (mem_sq_iff_linPart_eq_zero (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) hb)).1 hb, add_zero]
      exact (linPart_mem_span_image hS ha).2
    rw [eq_top_iff]
    intro v _
    have h0 := hX 0
    have h1 := hX 1
    rw [linPart_X_zero] at h0
    rw [linPart_X_one] at h1
    have hv : v = v.1 • ((1 : k), (0 : k)) + v.2 • ((0 : k), (1 : k)) := by
      refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp
    rw [hv]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h0) (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h1)
  · intro hspan
    refine le_antisymm (sup_le hSle (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num))) ?_
    have hXsup : ∀ i : Fin 2, (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ∈
        Ideal.span S ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := by
      intro i
      have hmem : linPart (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ∈
          Submodule.map linPart (Submodule.span k S) := by
        rw [← Submodule.span_image, hspan]; exact Submodule.mem_top
      obtain ⟨a, ha, hla⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.1 hmem
      have hsub : Submodule.span k S ≤
          Submodule.restrictScalars k (Ideal.span S) :=
        Submodule.span_le.mpr fun x hx => Ideal.subset_span hx
      have haI : a ∈ Ideal.span S := hsub ha
      have hamem : a ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := hSle haI
      have hdiff : (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) - a ∈
          (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := by
        refine (mem_sq_iff_linPart_eq_zero (Submodule.sub_mem _ (X_mem_maximalIdeal i) hamem)).2 ?_
        rw [map_sub, hla, sub_self]
      have hsum : (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) =
          a + ((MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) - a) := by ring
      rw [hsum]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.mem_sup_left haI) (Submodule.mem_sup_right hdiff)
    conv_lhs => rw [MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X k 2]
    rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact hXsup i

/-! ### The linear parts of the partial derivatives -/

/-- The linear part of `∂g/∂x_0` is the first partial derivative `(2a, b)` of the quadratic part
`(a, b, c)` of `g`. -/
theorem linPart_pderiv_zero (g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    linPart (pderiv (R := k) 0 g) = (2 * (quadPart g).1, (quadPart g).2.1) := by
  refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp only [linPart_apply, quadPart_apply]
  · rw [MvPowerSeries.coeff_pderiv (R := k) (i := 0) g (Finsupp.single 0 1),
      ← Finsupp.single_add, Finsupp.single_eq_same]
    push_cast
    ring
  · rw [MvPowerSeries.coeff_pderiv (R := k) (i := 0) g (Finsupp.single 1 1),
      add_comm (Finsupp.single (1 : Fin 2) 1)]
    simp

/-- The linear part of `∂g/∂x_1` is the second partial derivative `(b, 2c)` of the quadratic part
`(a, b, c)` of `g`. -/
theorem linPart_pderiv_one (g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    linPart (pderiv (R := k) 1 g) = ((quadPart g).2.1, 2 * (quadPart g).2.2) := by
  refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp only [linPart_apply, quadPart_apply]
  · rw [MvPowerSeries.coeff_pderiv (R := k) (i := 1) g (Finsupp.single 0 1)]
    simp
  · rw [MvPowerSeries.coeff_pderiv (R := k) (i := 1) g (Finsupp.single 1 1),
      ← Finsupp.single_add, Finsupp.single_eq_same]
    push_cast
    ring

/-- The partial derivatives of the members of a family generate, modulo `𝔪 ^ 2`, exactly the
derivative set of the space spanned by the quadratic parts of the family. -/
theorem span_linPart_image_pderiv_eq_span_derivSet {m : ℕ}
    (h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    Submodule.span k
        (linPart '' {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k | ∃ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m),
          x = pderiv (R := k) i (h j)}) =
      Submodule.span k (derivSet (Submodule.span k (Set.range (quadPart ∘ h)))) := by
  set V := Submodule.span k (Set.range (quadPart ∘ h)) with hV
  have hmemV : ∀ j, quadPart (h j) ∈ V := fun j =>
    Submodule.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro v ⟨x, ⟨i, j, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.subset_span ?_
    fin_cases i
    · exact ⟨quadPart (h j), hmemV j, Or.inl (linPart_pderiv_zero (h j))⟩
    · exact ⟨quadPart (h j), hmemV j, Or.inr (linPart_pderiv_one (h j))⟩
  · rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro v ⟨q, hq, hv⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun k).mp hq
    have hq1 : q.1 = ∑ j, c j * (quadPart (h j)).1 := by
      rw [← hc]
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Prod.fst_sum, Prod.smul_fst, smul_eq_mul]
    have hq21 : q.2.1 = ∑ j, c j * (quadPart (h j)).2.1 := by
      rw [← hc]
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Prod.snd_sum, Prod.fst_sum, Prod.smul_snd, Prod.smul_fst,
        smul_eq_mul]
    have hq22 : q.2.2 = ∑ j, c j * (quadPart (h j)).2.2 := by
      rw [← hc]
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, Prod.snd_sum, Prod.smul_snd, smul_eq_mul]
    have hgen : ∀ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m),
        linPart (pderiv (R := k) i (h j)) ∈ Submodule.span k
          (linPart '' {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k | ∃ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m),
            x = pderiv (R := k) i (h j)}) :=
      fun i j => Submodule.subset_span ⟨pderiv (R := k) i (h j), ⟨i, j, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    rcases hv with rfl | rfl
    · have hsum : (2 * q.1, q.2.1) =
          ∑ j, c j • linPart (pderiv (R := k) 0 (h j)) := by
        refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
          simp only [linPart_pderiv_zero, Prod.smul_fst, Prod.smul_snd, smul_eq_mul,
            Prod.fst_sum, Prod.snd_sum]
        · rw [hq1, Finset.mul_sum]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by ring
        · rw [hq21]
      rw [hsum]
      exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hgen 0 j)
    · have hsum : (q.2.1, 2 * q.2.2) =
          ∑ j, c j • linPart (pderiv (R := k) 1 (h j)) := by
        refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
          simp only [linPart_pderiv_one, Prod.smul_fst, Prod.smul_snd, smul_eq_mul,
            Prod.fst_sum, Prod.snd_sum]
        · rw [hq21]
        · rw [hq22, Finset.mul_sum]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by ring
      rw [hsum]
      exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hgen 1 j)

/-! ### The two-variable criterion in terms of the quadratic parts -/

/-- **The Jacobian criterion in two variables for a family of equations, in terms of quadratic
parts.** For a family `h` of elements of `𝔪 ^ 2` generating `J`, the partial derivatives of the
`h j` generate `𝔪` modulo `J` exactly when some element of `J` has nondegenerate quadratic
part. -/
@[sga "7 XV 1.2.7" "special case"]
theorem span_pderiv_sup_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_exists_nondegenerate {m : ℕ}
    (h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
    (hh : ∀ j, h j ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) :
    Ideal.span {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k | ∃ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m),
          x = pderiv (R := k) i (h j)} ⊔ Ideal.span (Set.range h) =
        maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) ↔
      ∃ g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range h), quadDisc (quadPart g) ≠ 0 := by
  set D : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
    {x | ∃ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m), x = pderiv (R := k) i (h j)} with hD
  set J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := Ideal.span (Set.range h) with hJ
  have hhm : ∀ j, h j ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
    fun j => Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) (hh j)
  have hJsq : J ≤ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := span_range_le_sq hh
  have hDm : ∀ x ∈ D, x ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := by
    rintro x ⟨i, j, rfl⟩
    refine mem_maximalIdeal_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero ?_
    rw [← MvPowerSeries.coeff_zero_eq_constantCoeff_apply,
      MvPowerSeries.coeff_pderiv (R := k) (i := i) (h j) 0, zero_add,
      ← linCoeff_eq_coeff, linCoeff_eq_zero_of_mem_sq i (hh j), zero_mul]
  have hDle : Ideal.span D ≤ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := Ideal.span_le.mpr hDm
  -- the defining ideal may be traded for the square of the maximal ideal
  have hstep1 : (Ideal.span D ⊔ J = maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ↔
      (Ideal.span D ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 =
        maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) := by
    constructor
    · intro hsup
      refine le_antisymm (sup_le hDle (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num))) ?_
      calc maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) = Ideal.span D ⊔ J := hsup.symm
        _ ≤ Ideal.span D ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 :=
            sup_le_sup_left hJsq _
    · intro hsup
      refine eq_maximalIdeal_of_le_sup_sq (sup_le hDle (hJsq.trans
        (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num)))) ?_
      calc maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
          = Ideal.span D ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := hsup.symm
        _ ≤ (Ideal.span D ⊔ J) ⊔ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 :=
            sup_le_sup_right le_sup_left _
  rw [hstep1, sup_sq_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_span_linPart hDm, hD,
    span_linPart_image_pderiv_eq_span_derivSet h,
    span_derivSet_eq_top_iff_exists_nondegenerate]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨q, hq, hdisc⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun k).mp hq
    refine ⟨∑ j, c j • h j, ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ =>
        Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩)
    · rw [map_sum]
      simp only [map_smul]
      rw [show (∑ j, c j • quadPart (h j)) = q from hc]
      exact hdisc
  · rintro ⟨g, hg, hdisc⟩
    refine ⟨quadPart g, ?_, hdisc⟩
    rw [Set.range_comp]
    exact (quadPart_mem_span_image (Set.forall_mem_range.2 hh) hg).2


/-! ### Quadratic parts of products -/

private theorem X_mul_X_eq_monomial (i j : Fin 2) :
    (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X j =
      MvPowerSeries.monomial (Finsupp.single i 1 + Finsupp.single j 1) 1 := by
  rw [MvPowerSeries.X_def, MvPowerSeries.X_def, MvPowerSeries.monomial_mul_monomial, mul_one]

private theorem X_mul_X_mem_sq (i j : Fin 2) :
    (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X j ∈
      (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 :=
  mul_mem_sq (X_mem_maximalIdeal i) (X_mem_maximalIdeal j)

/-- The quadratic part of `x_0 * x_0` is `(1, 0, 0)`. -/
theorem quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_zero :
    quadPart ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 0) =
      (1, 0, 0) := by
  rw [X_mul_X_eq_monomial, ← Finsupp.single_add]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;>
    simp [quadPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial, Finsupp.ext_iff, Fin.forall_fin_two]

/-- The quadratic part of `x_0 * x_1` is `(0, 1, 0)`. -/
theorem quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_one :
    quadPart ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) =
      (0, 1, 0) := by
  rw [X_mul_X_eq_monomial]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;>
    simp [quadPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial, Finsupp.ext_iff, Fin.forall_fin_two]

/-- The quadratic part of `x_1 * x_1` is `(0, 0, 1)`. -/
theorem quadPart_X_mul_X_one_one :
    quadPart ((MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) =
      (0, 0, 1) := by
  rw [X_mul_X_eq_monomial, ← Finsupp.single_add]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;>
    simp [quadPart_apply, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial, Finsupp.ext_iff, Fin.forall_fin_two]

/-- An element of `𝔪` is its linear part plus an element of `𝔪 ^ 2`. -/
theorem sub_linear_mem_sq {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    g - ((linPart g).1 • (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) +
        (linPart g).2 • (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ∈
      (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := by
  have h := sub_linearPart_mem_sq
    ((Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field g).1
      hg)
  have hrw : (∑ j : Fin 2, linCoeff j g • (MvPowerSeries.X j : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) =
      (linPart g).1 • (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) +
        (linPart g).2 • (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := by
    rw [Fin.sum_univ_two, linCoeff_eq_coeff, linCoeff_eq_coeff, linPart_apply]
  rwa [hrw] at h

/-- **The quadratic part of a product of two elements of `𝔪`** is the product of their linear
parts, as binary quadratic forms. -/
theorem quadPart_mul (s t : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
    (hs : s ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k))
    (ht : t ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    quadPart (s * t) =
      ((linPart s).1 * (linPart t).1,
        (linPart s).1 * (linPart t).2 + (linPart s).2 * (linPart t).1,
        (linPart s).2 * (linPart t).2) := by
  set p := (linPart s).1 with hp
  set q := (linPart s).2 with hq
  set p' := (linPart t).1 with hp'
  set q' := (linPart t).2 with hq'
  set sl : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
    p • (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) +
      q • (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) with hsl
  set tl : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
    p' • (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) +
      q' • (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) with htl
  have hsq : s - sl ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := sub_linear_mem_sq hs
  have htq : t - tl ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := sub_linear_mem_sq ht
  have hslm : sl ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := by
    have := Submodule.sub_mem _ hs
      (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) hsq)
    simpa using this
  have hcube : (s - sl) * t + sl * (t - tl) ∈
      (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 3 :=
    Submodule.add_mem _ (mul_comm t _ ▸ mul_mem_cube ht hsq) (mul_mem_cube hslm htq)
  have hsplit : s * t = sl * tl + ((s - sl) * t + sl * (t - tl)) := by ring
  rw [hsplit, map_add, quadPart_eq_zero_of_mem_cube hcube, add_zero]
  have hprod : sl * tl =
      algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (p * p') *
          ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 0) +
        algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (p * q' + q * p') *
          ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) +
        algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (q * q') *
          ((MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) := by
    simp only [hsl, htl, Algebra.smul_def, map_add, map_mul]
    ring
  have hcc : ∀ a : k,
      MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) a) = a := by
    intro a
    rw [MvPowerSeries.algebraMap_apply]
    simp
  rw [hprod]
  simp only [map_add, quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 0 0),
    quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 0 1),
    quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 1 1),
    quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_zero, quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_one, quadPart_X_mul_X_one_one, hcc]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;> simp

/-- An element of `𝔪 ^ 2` in two variables is a combination of the three quadratic monomials,
with the constant terms of the coefficients reading off its quadratic part. -/
theorem exists_quadratic_decomposition {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hg : g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2) :
    ∃ u v w : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k,
      g = u * ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 0) +
            v * ((MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) +
            w * ((MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) * MvPowerSeries.X 1) ∧
        MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff u = (quadPart g).1 ∧
        MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff v = (quadPart g).2.1 ∧
        MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff w = (quadPart g).2.2 := by
  have hgm : g ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
    Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) hg
  have hg0 : MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff g = (0 : k) :=
    (Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field _).1
      hgm
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hPsum⟩ :=
    Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero g hg0
  have hPm : ∀ i, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (P i) = (0 : k) := by
    intro i
    rw [hP i]
    have := linCoeff_eq_zero_of_mem_sq i hg
    rwa [linCoeff_eq_coeff] at this
  obtain ⟨U, -, hUsum⟩ :=
    Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero (P 0) (hPm 0)
  obtain ⟨W, -, hWsum⟩ :=
    Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero (P 1) (hPm 1)
  refine ⟨U 0, U 1 + W 0, W 1, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hPsum, Fin.sum_univ_two, hUsum, hWsum, Fin.sum_univ_two, Fin.sum_univ_two]
    ring
  all_goals
    rw [hPsum, Fin.sum_univ_two, hUsum, hWsum, Fin.sum_univ_two, Fin.sum_univ_two,
      show (MvPowerSeries.X 0 * (MvPowerSeries.X 0 * U 0 + MvPowerSeries.X 1 * U 1) +
          MvPowerSeries.X 1 * (MvPowerSeries.X 0 * W 0 + MvPowerSeries.X 1 * W 1) :
            MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) =
        U 0 * (MvPowerSeries.X 0 * MvPowerSeries.X 0) +
          (U 1 + W 0) * (MvPowerSeries.X 0 * MvPowerSeries.X 1) +
          W 1 * (MvPowerSeries.X 1 * MvPowerSeries.X 1) from by ring,
      ]
    simp only [map_add, quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 0 0),
      quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 0 1),
      quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq (X_mul_X_mem_sq (k := k) 1 1),
      quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_zero, quadPart_X_mul_X_zero_one, quadPart_X_mul_X_one_one]
    simp

/-! ### The nondegenerate quadratic relation on the quotient -/

private theorem mem_maximalIdeal_quotient {J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)] {z : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hz : z ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) :
    algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J) z ∈
      maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J) :=
  Ideal.mem_comap.mp (by
    rw [maximalIdeal_comap
      (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J))]
    exact hz)

private theorem mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient
    {J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)] {z : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k}
    (hz : algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J) z ∈
      maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)) :
    z ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) := by
  rw [← maximalIdeal_comap
    (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J))]
  exact Ideal.mem_comap.mpr hz

private theorem residue_algebraMap_eq_zero_iff {J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)] (z : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)
        (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J) z) = 0 ↔
      MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff z = (0 : k) := by
  rw [residue_eq_zero_iff, ←
    Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.mem_maximalIdeal_iff_constantCoeff_eq_zero_field]
  exact ⟨mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient, mem_maximalIdeal_quotient⟩

/-- The residue of `4 a c - b ^ 2` in `k[[x_0, x_1]] / J` vanishes exactly when the constant term
of `4 a c - b ^ 2` does. -/
private theorem residue_disc_eq_zero_iff {J : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)}
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)] (a b c : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :
    residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J)
        (4 * algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ J) a *
          algebraMap _ _ c - (algebraMap _ _ b) ^ 2) = 0 ↔
      4 * MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff a * MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff c -
        MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff b ^ 2 = (0 : k) := by
  have := residue_algebraMap_eq_zero_iff (J := J) (4 * a * c - b ^ 2)
  simpa only [map_sub, map_mul, map_pow, map_ofNat] using this

/-- **The two-variable Jacobian criterion meets Tag 0C49's quadratic relation.** For a family `h`
of elements of `𝔪 ^ 2` in `k[[x_0, x_1]]` generating `J`, some element of `J` has nondegenerate
quadratic part exactly when `k[[x_0, x_1]] / J` carries a nondegenerate quadratic relation on its
cotangent space. -/
theorem exists_nondegenerate_quadPart_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation {m : ℕ}
    (h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
    (hh : ∀ j, h j ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2)
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))] :
    (∃ g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range h), quadDisc (quadPart g) ≠ 0) ↔
      HasNodalQuadraticRelation (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) := by
  classical
  have hJsq := span_range_le_sq hh
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨g, hgJ, hdisc⟩
    have hgsq : g ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := hJsq hgJ
    obtain ⟨u, v, w, hgdec, hu, hv, hw⟩ := exists_quadratic_decomposition hgsq
    refine (hasNodalQuadraticRelation_iff_exists_basis _).2 ?_
    refine ⟨⟨algebraMap _ _ (MvPowerSeries.X 0), mem_maximalIdeal_quotient (X_mem_maximalIdeal 0)⟩,
      ⟨algebraMap _ _ (MvPowerSeries.X 1), mem_maximalIdeal_quotient (X_mem_maximalIdeal 1)⟩,
      IsLocalRing.basisCotangentSpaceQuotient _ hJsq
        (Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.basisCotangentSpaceX Equiv.ulift),
      algebraMap _ _ u, algebraMap _ _ v, algebraMap _ _ w, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [IsLocalRing.basisCotangentSpaceQuotient_apply,
        Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.basisCotangentSpaceX_apply,
        IsLocalRing.cotangentSpaceQuotientEquiv_toCotangent]
      rfl
    · rw [IsLocalRing.basisCotangentSpaceQuotient_apply,
        Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.basisCotangentSpaceX_apply,
        IsLocalRing.cotangentSpaceQuotientEquiv_toCotangent]
      rfl
    · rw [Ne, residue_disc_eq_zero_iff, hu, hv, hw]
      exact hdisc
    · set φ := algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) with hφ
      have hzero : φ g = 0 := by
        rw [hφ, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
        exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 hgJ
      have hcalc : φ u * (φ (MvPowerSeries.X 0)) ^ 2 +
          φ v * φ (MvPowerSeries.X 0) * φ (MvPowerSeries.X 1) +
          φ w * (φ (MvPowerSeries.X 1)) ^ 2 = φ g := by
        rw [hgdec]
        simp only [map_add, map_mul]
        ring
      have hmem : φ g ∈
          (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))) ^ 3 := by
        rw [hzero]
        exact Submodule.zero_mem _
      rw [← hcalc] at hmem
      exact hmem
  · intro hrel
    obtain ⟨x, y, e, a, b, c, hx, hy, hnd, hm⟩ :=
      (hasNodalQuadraticRelation_iff_exists_basis _).1 hrel
    have hsurj := IsLocalRing.surjective_algebraMap_quotient (Ideal.span (Set.range h))
    obtain ⟨xt, hxt⟩ := hsurj (x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
    obtain ⟨yt, hyt⟩ := hsurj (y : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
    obtain ⟨at', rfl⟩ := hsurj a
    obtain ⟨bt, rfl⟩ := hsurj b
    obtain ⟨ct, rfl⟩ := hsurj c
    have hxtm : xt ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
      mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient (by rw [hxt]; exact x.2)
    have hytm : yt ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
      mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient (by rw [hyt]; exact y.2)
    -- the relation lifts to an element of the ideal, up to a term of `𝔪 ^ 3`
    have hmapcube : (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))) ^ 3 =
        Ideal.map (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)))
          ((maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 3) := by
      rw [Ideal.map_pow, IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ hsurj]
    rw [hmapcube] at hm
    obtain ⟨ρ, hρcube, hρ⟩ := (Ideal.mem_map_iff_of_surjective _ hsurj).1 hm
    set g : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
      at' * (xt * xt) + bt * (xt * yt) + ct * (yt * yt) - ρ with hgdef
    have hsqxx := mul_mem_sq hxtm hxtm
    have hsqxy := mul_mem_sq hxtm hytm
    have hsqyy := mul_mem_sq hytm hytm
    have hgJ : g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range h) := by
      rw [← IsLocalRing.ker_algebraMap_quotient (Ideal.span (Set.range h)), RingHom.mem_ker,
        hgdef, map_sub, hρ]
      simp only [map_add, map_mul, hxt, hyt]
      ring
    -- the quadratic part of `g`
    set p := (linPart xt).1 with hp
    set q := (linPart xt).2 with hq
    set r := (linPart yt).1 with hr
    set t := (linPart yt).2 with ht
    set α := MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff at' with hα
    set β := MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff bt with hβ
    set γ := MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff ct with hγ
    have hquad : quadPart g =
        (α * (p * p) + β * (p * r) + γ * (r * r),
          α * (p * q + q * p) + β * (p * t + q * r) + γ * (r * t + t * r),
          α * (q * q) + β * (q * t) + γ * (t * t)) := by
      rw [hgdef, map_sub, quadPart_eq_zero_of_mem_cube hρcube, sub_zero, map_add, map_add,
        quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq hsqxx, quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq hsqxy,
        quadPart_mul_of_mem_sq hsqyy, quadPart_mul _ _ hxtm hxtm,
        quadPart_mul _ _ hxtm hytm, quadPart_mul _ _ hytm hytm]
      refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_) <;> simp [hα, hβ, hγ, hp, hq, hr, ht]
    -- nondegeneracy of the lifted coefficients
    have hndα : 4 * α * γ - β ^ 2 ≠ 0 := fun hzero =>
      hnd ((residue_disc_eq_zero_iff at' bt ct).2 hzero)
    -- the two lifted linear parts are independent
    have hli : LinearIndependent
        (ResidueField (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)))
        ![(maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent x,
          (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent y] := by
      have h2 := e.linearIndependent.comp
        (fun i : Fin 2 => (ULift.up i : BinaryIndex
          (ResidueField (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)))))
        (fun i j hij => by simpa using hij)
      have hfun : (fun i : Fin 2 => e (ULift.up i)) =
          ![(maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent x,
            (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
              Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent y] := by
        funext i
        fin_cases i
        · simpa using hx
        · simpa using hy
      simp only [Function.comp_def] at h2
      rw [hfun] at h2
      exact h2
    have hdet : p * t - q * r ≠ 0 := by
      intro hD
      obtain ⟨μ, ν, hμν, h1, h2⟩ := exists_ne_zero_of_det_eq_zero p r q t
        (by linear_combination hD)
      set z : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k := μ • xt + ν • yt with hz
      have hzm : z ∈ maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) :=
        Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ _ hxtm)
          (Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ _ hytm)
      have hzsq : z ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2 := by
        refine (mem_sq_iff_linPart_eq_zero hzm).2 ?_
        rw [hz, map_add, map_smul, map_smul]
        refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
          simp only [Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add, Prod.smul_fst, Prod.smul_snd, smul_eq_mul,
            Prod.fst_zero, Prod.snd_zero, ← hp, ← hq, ← hr, ← ht]
        · linear_combination h1
        · linear_combination h2
      have hzQ : algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) z ∈
            (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))) ^ 2 := by
        rw [← IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ hsurj, ← Ideal.map_pow]
        exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hzsq
      have hcoe : (⟨algebraMap _ _ z, (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num) hzQ)⟩ :
            maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))) =
          (algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) μ) • x +
            (algebraMap k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) ν) • y := by
        apply Subtype.ext
        simp only [Submodule.coe_add, SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul]
        rw [hz, map_add, Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, map_mul, hxt, hyt,
          ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) _ μ,
          ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) _ ν]
      have hzerocot :
          residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
              (algebraMap k _ μ) •
            (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
              Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent x +
          residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
              (algebraMap k _ ν) •
            (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸
              Ideal.span (Set.range h))).toCotangent y = 0 := by
        rw [Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.residue_smul_toCotangent,
          Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.residue_smul_toCotangent,
          ← map_add, ← hcoe, Ideal.toCotangent_eq_zero]
        exact hzQ
      obtain ⟨hμ0, hν0⟩ := LinearIndependent.pair_iff.mp hli _ _ hzerocot
      have hkey : ∀ s : k,
          residue (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
            (algebraMap k _ s) = 0 → s = 0 := by
        intro s hs
        rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) _ s,
          residue_algebraMap_eq_zero_iff, MvPowerSeries.algebraMap_apply] at hs
        simpa using hs
      rcases hμν with hne | hne
      · exact hne (hkey μ hμ0)
      · exact hne (hkey ν hν0)
    refine ⟨g, hgJ, ?_⟩
    rw [hquad, quadDisc_apply]
    have hid : 4 * (α * (p * p) + β * (p * r) + γ * (r * r)) *
          (α * (q * q) + β * (q * t) + γ * (t * t)) -
        (α * (p * q + q * p) + β * (p * t + q * r) + γ * (r * t + t * r)) ^ 2 =
          (4 * α * γ - β ^ 2) * (p * t - q * r) ^ 2 := by ring
    rw [hid]
    exact mul_ne_zero hndα (pow_ne_zero 2 hdet)

/-! ### The criterion in the form Tag 0C4C states it -/

/-- **The Jacobian criterion of Tag 0C4C in two variables, for an arbitrary family of
equations.** For a family `h` of elements of `𝔪 ^ 2` in `k[[x_0, x_1]]` generating `J`, the
Jacobian-minor ideal of Tag 0C4B at `r = 1` is the maximal ideal of `k[[x_0, x_1]] / J` exactly
when that quotient carries a nondegenerate quadratic relation on its cotangent space — that is,
exactly when it satisfies the cotangent-space half of Tag 0C49.

Together with `Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_tfae_of_jacobianMinorIdeal_iff` this is Tag 0C4C for
`n = 2` and `I ⊆ 𝔪 ^ 2`. -/
theorem jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation {m : ℕ}
    (h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
    (hh : ∀ j, h j ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2)
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))] :
    jacobianMinorIdealModulo (Ideal.span (Set.range h)) h 1 =
        maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) ↔
      HasNodalQuadraticRelation (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) := by
  have hJsq := span_range_le_sq hh
  have hminor : minorIdeal (fun (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m) => pderiv (R := k) i (h j)) 1 =
      Ideal.span {x : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k | ∃ (i : Fin 2) (j : Fin m),
        x = pderiv (R := k) i (h j)} := minorIdeal_one _
  rw [jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq_maximalIdeal_iff _
      (hJsq.trans (Ideal.pow_le_self (n := 2) (by norm_num))) h 1,
    hminor, span_pderiv_sup_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_exists_nondegenerate h hh,
    exists_nondegenerate_quadPart_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation h hh]

/-- **Tag 0C4C for two variables and a defining ideal inside `𝔪 ^ 2`.** For `A = k[[x_0, x_1]]`
and `I = (h_1, …, h_m) ⊆ 𝔪_A ^ 2`, the three conditions of Tag 0C4C are equivalent: `A/I` is a
nodal `k`-algebra; `A/I` is reduced and the `1 × 1` Jacobian minors generate `𝔪_{A/I}`; `A/I` has
depth one and the same Jacobian condition holds.

This is the case `n = 2` of Tag 0C4C, obtained from
`Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation` and
`Stacks.Curves.isNodalAlgebra_tfae_of_jacobianMinorIdeal_iff`. The general case needs, in
addition, the reduction of an arbitrary `n` and an arbitrary `I ⊆ 𝔪_A` to this one: a regular
system of parameters adapted to the image of `I` in the cotangent space, which Tag 0C4B
(`Stacks.Curves.jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq`) and
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.extend_partial_rsop_field` make available, followed by
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.quotient_initial_vars`. -/
theorem isNodalAlgebra_jacobianMinorIdeal_tfae_two_of_le_sq {m : ℕ}
    (h : Fin m → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)
    (hh : ∀ j, h j ∈ (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k)) ^ 2)
    [IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))] :
    List.TFAE [
      IsNodalAlgebra k (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)),
      IsReduced (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) ∧
        jacobianMinorIdealModulo (Ideal.span (Set.range h)) h (2 - 1) =
          maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)),
      Module.depth (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))
          (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)))
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h)) = 1 ∧
        jacobianMinorIdealModulo (Ideal.span (Set.range h)) h (2 - 1) =
          maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range h))] :=
  isNodalAlgebra_tfae_of_jacobianMinorIdeal_iff (Ideal.span (Set.range h)) h
    (jacobianMinorIdealModulo_eq_maximalIdeal_iff_hasNodalQuadraticRelation h hh)

end Stacks.Curves

